-- title:
--   Cocommutative generated norm-one torus Hopf algebra inside an ambient one
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero, let $c \in K$ with $c \neq 0$ and $c$ not a square in $K$, and let $B$ be a commutative ring carrying the structure of a $K$-Hopf algebra. Suppose given $u, v \in B$ satisfying the relation $u^2 - c v^2 = 1$ (with $c$ read in $B$ via the structure map) and the comultiplication formulas $\Delta(u) = u \otimes u + c \cdot (v \otimes v)$ and $\Delta(v) = u \otimes v + v \otimes u$ in $B \otimes_K B$, and suppose that for every pair $(w, z)$ of elements of the algebraic closure $\overline{K}$ with $w^2 - c z^2 = 1$ there is exactly one $K$-algebra homomorphism $f : B \to \overline{K}$ with $f(u) = w$ and $f(v) = z$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a commutative ring $B_0$ with a $K$-Hopf algebra structure whose comultiplication is cocommutative, together with elements $u_0, v_0 \in B_0$ such that the $K$-subalgebra generated by $u_0$ and $v_0$ is all of $B_0$, the relation $u_0^2 - c v_0^2 = 1$ holds, the same two comultiplication formulas hold for $u_0, v_0$, and every $(w, z) \in \overline{K}^2$ with $w^2 - c z^2 = 1$ is hit by a unique $K$-algebra homomorphism $B_0 \to \overline{K}$ sending $u_0 \mapsto w$ and $v_0 \mapsto z$.
--
--   The data $(B_0, u_0, v_0)$ is a presentation of the coordinate ring of the norm-one torus $T = \mathrm{Res}^{(1)}_{K(\sqrt{c})/K}\mathbb{G}_m$ as a Hopf algebra generated by its two standard coordinates, extracted from an ambient Hopf algebra with the same generators and the same $\overline{K}$-points. It is used by [`HopfAlgebra.exists_cocomm_adjoin_nTorsion_quotient_of_normOneTorus_generators`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_cocomm_adjoin_nTorsion_quotient_of_normOneTorus_generators), which passes to the $n$-torsion quotient of this torus.
-- source:
